From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:58:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: read a tessellation control shader's own gl_PerVertex
 output

A tessellation control shader may read any patch vertex's gl_Position or
gl_PointSize back after a barrier, and TGSI spells that as a source in
the output file whose dimension names the vertex.  get_source_info()
recognised only gl_ClipDistance in that block and left the source string
untouched for every other member, so the instruction silently reused the
operand string the previous instruction had built -- typically the
address register feeding the very read that was dropped.  A guest that
lands a user varying in the position slot, as an OpenGL ES 3.2
tessellation control shader with no other per-vertex output does, then
read arithmetic on the vertex index instead of the value stored there.

KHR-GLES32.core.tessellation_shader.tessellation_shader_tc_barriers.
barrier_guarded_read_write_calls failed with exactly the sum of the
float bit patterns of the four indices it should have summed values for.

Emit the block read the way the input path already emits gl_in[].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_shader.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
index d57aa56633949cf68a824cf78d8350a669339aa3..ea3d999e16c0364cf341d008eb8f398d5ec6777b 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -5095,6 +5095,16 @@ get_source_info(struct dump_ctx *ctx,
                      snprintf(clip_indirect, sizeof(clip_indirect), "+ %d", src->Register.Index - output->first);
                }
                strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "clip_dist_temp[%d%s]", output->sid, clip_indirect);
+            } else {
+               /* The block is only ever a tessellation control shader's
+                * gl_out[], and such a shader may read the member back from any
+                * vertex of the patch, so name the vertex the register gives.
+                * Without this the source string is never written and the
+                * instruction silently reuses the previous one's operand. */
+               strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%s(vec4(%sgl_out%s.%s)%s)",
+                          get_string(srcstypeprefix), prefix,
+                          arrayname[0] != '\0' ? arrayname : "[gl_InvocationID]",
+                          output->glsl_name, swizzle);
             }
          } else if (output->name == TGSI_SEMANTIC_GENERIC) {
             struct vrend_shader_io *io = ctx->generic_ios.output_range.used ? &ctx->generic_ios.output_range.io : &ctx->outputs[j];
